From 77b71f78b216efea67651394267e860eff081877 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:02:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(contour): enter every wall-side ring by the ramp, not the
 pass link plunge

An outside 2D Contour with entry Ramp or Helix entered only the first ring
of each level by its entry. Each later ring at the same level took the
pass link: lift, cross, and an axial plunge at the plunge feed, with no
note. `contour_link::ring_entry` (from #3834, bore side) now applies on
the wall side too, for the Ramp and Helix arms. The ring then takes the
wall-side ramp of #3833 through `engage_level`, and the traverse rides
the pass link plane (`Step::traverse`). The wall-side Arc entry, tabbed
levels and the Plunge entry keep their old paths.

Pinned by every_outside_ring_of_several_parts_is_entered_by_the_wall_side_ramp.

Fixes #3917

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
